{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And remember.</b> We find נעורים, עלומים, זקונים — all of them are masculine language; only בחורותיך departs from the pattern. Some say they are two [different] roots, and they interpret (Numbers 11:28) 'Moses' young men' (מבחוריו) as though it were מבחורותיו, for all [forms of] בחורים, if they are joined [ grammatically ], do not change." "<b>The evil days.</b> They are the days of old age for an old man, and the days of illness for everyone — meaning the illness of which one dies."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "Resolved the parenthetical citation from משר' משה; 'משרת' appears to be abbreviated."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:15.255602953Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}